# Soroban Keeper Network React example — configuration template.
#
# ⚠️  DEV-ONLY PATTERN. This demo signs with a secret key loaded into the
# browser bundle for simplicity, so the focus stays on composing the React
# hooks rather than wallet integration. Vite inlines every VITE_* value into
# the built JS in PLAIN TEXT — anyone can read it from the page source. Never
# do this with a real account's secret key or in anything you deploy. A real
# dApp should sign with a browser wallet extension instead — see
# ../wallet-signing/registerTaskWithFreighter.ts for that pattern.

# testnet, futurenet, or mainnet — matches NetworkName in ../../src/network.ts.
VITE_NETWORK=testnet

# Deployed KeeperRegistry contract address (C...). The placeholder below is
# format-valid but not a real deployment; every hook will report empty/zero
# results against it rather than erroring, so the app is safe to explore
# without a real contract, but "Register" will fail against the network.
VITE_REGISTRY_CONTRACT_ID=CAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAD2KM

# Demo-only signing key (starts with S...). The placeholder below is a
# syntactically valid, unfunded testnet seed — safe to leave as-is to explore
# the read-only hooks (useTaskEvents, useKeeperBalance); replace it with your
# own funded testnet key to actually exercise useRegisterTask.
VITE_DEMO_SECRET_KEY=SBGWKM3CD4IL47QN6X54N6Y33T3JDNVI6AIJ6CD5IM47HG3IG4O36XCU
